Debug line only: which check makes btusb drop an incoming SCO fragment.

Not for upstream submission. The kernel logs "corrupted SCO packet"
(btusb_isoc_complete) when btusb_recv_isoc() returns -EILSEQ, for either of
two reasons: the header's length exceeds the skb's tailroom, or the header's
handle is not a live SCO/eSCO connection (a lost fragment, or data still
arriving after the link was deleted). This adds one dynamic-debug site on that
branch, off unless enabled:

  echo 'module btusb func btusb_recv_isoc +p' > /sys/kernel/debug/dynamic_debug/control

It runs in URB completion context, but only on the error path (U8 recorded
six per link). Against Ubuntu's 7.0.0-34 source (cache/ubuntu-7.0.0-34).

--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c
@@ -1407,6 +1407,11 @@
 
 			if (skb_tailroom(skb) < hci_skb_expect(skb) ||
 			    !btusb_validate_sco_handle(data->hdev, hdr)) {
+				bt_dev_dbg(data->hdev,
+					   "dropped SCO fragment: handle 0x%4.4x dlen %u tailroom %u valid-handle %d",
+					   hci_handle(__le16_to_cpu(hdr->handle)), hdr->dlen,
+					   skb_tailroom(skb),
+					   btusb_validate_sco_handle(data->hdev, hdr));
 				kfree_skb(skb);
 				skb = NULL;
 
